			"Message": "build(deps-dev): bump @types/node from 25.9.0 to 25.9.1\n\nBumps [@types/node](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/node) from 25.9.0 to 25.9.1.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/node)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: \"@types/node\"\n  dependency-version: 25.9.1\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>",
			"SHA": "a02f5dfb079adbe479ba81a57445923acc9aba09"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T00:37:06Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				751,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(tauri): Implement dual-track IPC routing with Tier-based fallback\n\nIntroduced a tiered IPC strategy to support both the existing 'Mountain' route and a new 'Node'/'Cocoon' fallback path within the Tauri channel implementation. This change addresses the need for flexible backend routing during the transition period between architectural tiers.\n\nKey modifications include:\n- Added `_TierIPC` configuration logic to determine the active IPC strategy via environment variables or global constants, defaulting to 'Mountain'.\n- Implemented `_InvokeViaNode` helper to forward requests to the 'Cocoon' backend using the `MountainIPCInvoke` mechanism or direct Node method invocation.\n- Updated `TauriChannel` to route calls through the Node path when `_TierIPC` is set to 'Node' or 'NodeDeferred', ensuring graceful fallback if the primary 'Mountain' route is unavailable or intentionally deferred.\n- Preserved existing behavior by defaulting to the standard `InvokeMountain` flow unless explicitly configured otherwise.\n\nThis implementation ensures backward compatibility while enabling incremental adoption of the new Node-based communication layer.",
			"SHA": "22b14ca67fe8c26b4f9c033d47974d6f93414801"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
